    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "737-700\nAlaska Airlines\nAIRCRAFT SAFETY INFORMATION\nIF YOU ARE SEATED IN AN EXIT ROW\nATTENTION: IF YOU ARE SEATED IN AN EXIT ROW AND CANNOT\nUNDERSTAND CREW COMMANDS OR THE INFORMATION ON THE CARD,\nPLEASE CONTACT A FLIGHT ATTENDANT.\nATTENTION: SI VOUS ÊTES ASSIS PRÈS D'UNE ISSUE DE SECOURS ET\nNE COMPRENEZ PAS LES INSTRUCTIONS DE L'EQUIPAGE OU LES\nINFORMATIONS QUI SE TROUVENT SUR CE FORMULAIRE, VOUS ETES\nPRIES DE BIEN VOULOIR VOUS METTRE EN CONTACT AVEC LE\nPERSONNEL DU BORD.\nВНИМАНИЕ: ЕСЛИ ВАШЕ МЕСТО - В РЯДУ АВАРИЙНОГО ВЫХОДА,\nА ВЫ НЕ ПОНИМАЕТЕ КОМАНД ЭКИПАЖА И НЕ МОЖЕТЕ\nПРОЧИТАТЬ ИНСТРУКЦИИ НА ДАННОЙ КАРТОЧКЕ, ПОЖАЛУЙСТА,\nОБРАТИТЕСЬ К БОРТПРОВОДНИКУ.\nACHTUNG: FALL SICH IHR SITZ IN EINER REIHE AN EINEM DER\nAUSGANGE BEFINDET UND SIE SCHWIERIGKEITEN HABEN, DIE\nANWEISUNGEN DER BESATZUNG ODER DIE INFORMATIONEN AUF\nDIESER KARTE ZU VERSTEHEN, SETZEN SIE SICH BITTE MIT EINEM\nFLUGBEGLEITER IN VERBINDUNG.\nATENCION: SI USTED ESTÁ SENTADO EN UNA FILA DE SALIDA Y NO\nENTIENDE LAS INDICACIONES DE LA TRIPULACIÓN O LA INFORMACIÓN\nEN ESTA TARJETA, POR FAVOR PONGASE EN CONTACTO CON ALGUIEN\nDE LA TRIPULACION DE SERVICIO.\nWhen you are seated in an exit row, you may be called upon to open the exit and\nassist fellow passengers in exiting the aircraft if a crewmember is unavailable to\ndo so. Because of this, and for the benefit of all passengers, Federal Law\nrequires that passengers seated in the exit rows must meet the following criteria.\nIF YOU ARE SEATED IN AN EXIT ROW\nPLEASE ASK TO BE RESEATED IF:\n• You lack sufficient mobility, strength or dexterity in both arms and hands, and\nboth legs to expeditiously reach the emergency exit, remove obstructions,\nmanipulate the emergency exit and exit slide mechanisms, open and store the\nexit door, exit expeditiously, stabilize the escape slide, and assist others in\ngetting off the escape slide.\n• You do not understand these instructions, or lack sufficient visual capacity\n(require aids beyond contact lenses or glasses) or aural capacity require aids\nbeyond a hearing aid to understand these and crewmember instructions or to\nimpart information orally to others.\n•You have a responsibility such as to a small child or a nondiscernible condition\nthat might prevent you from performing these functions or a condition that might\ncause you to suffer bodily harm while performing these functions.\n•You do not want to perform these functions.\n•You are less than 15 years of age.\nEXIT OPERATION: ASSESS OUTSIDE CONDITIONS-IF OPENING EXIT\nINCREASES THE HAZARD TO PASSENGERS, DO NOT OPEN.\nFor your safety obey \"Fasten Seatbelt\" and \"No Smoking\" signs.\nFollow all instructions given by crew members.",
      "0-88G (7/99) Copyright © 1999 SAFEAIR, Olympia, WA., (360)754-5837. All Rights Reserved. www.safeair-usa.com",
      "OK\nOK\u0026\nOKS\n2\n3\nSAFELY\nSTAY SEATED WITH\nSEATBELT FASTENED\nPULL\nBEEa"
    ],
